      "title": "Legacy Note: Troubleshooting TLS Handshakes and DNS Failures in Role Manager",
      "content_summary": "Addresses TLS handshake errors, DNS lookup failures, and timeouts in Role Manager caused by network configuration or incorrect DNS settings. Recommends DNS correction and load balancer reconfiguration.",
      "content_body": "1. If Role Manager agents fail to connect with a TLS handshake error, verify the system-level DNS configuration first, as outdated proxy settings often mask the underlying lookup failure.\n2. For persistent timeouts, check the load balancer rules; legacy versions required manual reconfiguration of the virtual IP to bypass SSL termination issues.\n3. Ensure that the DNS records are corrected to point to the active cluster node, as the old automatic failover feature was not enabled by default in previous builds.\n4. Note: These steps apply to deployments prior to the introduction of the unified connectivity gateway."
